import{_t as e,it as t,n,rt as r}from"./chunks/framework.B5d4da8a.js";var i=JSON.parse(`{"title":"Plan 0025 — finishing the minting stack and the substrate","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"graphopt/project/plans/0025-minting-and-substrate.md","filePath":"vendored/graphopt/project/plans/0025-minting-and-substrate.md"}`),a={name:`graphopt/project/plans/0025-minting-and-substrate.md`};function o(n,i,a,o,s,c){return e(),r(`div`,null,[...i[0]||=[t(`<h1 id="plan-0025-—-finishing-the-minting-stack-and-the-substrate" tabindex="-1">Plan 0025 — finishing the minting stack and the substrate <a class="header-anchor" href="#plan-0025-—-finishing-the-minting-stack-and-the-substrate" aria-label="Permalink to “Plan 0025 — finishing the minting stack and the substrate”">​</a></h1><p>Depends on: ADR 0007 (semantic-atom minting — measured), ADR 0008 (combinator presentation — bridge gates 1–2 PASS, gate 3 open), plan 0024 (form-level proposer / vocabulary minting), plan 0012 (bounded-error rewrites).</p><h2 id="motivation" tabindex="-1">Motivation <a class="header-anchor" href="#motivation" aria-label="Permalink to “Motivation”">​</a></h2><p>This cycle closed the minting loop far enough to ship: <code>mul_unsq_nat</code> is the first law minted from a <em>corpus op-tuple</em> and it is in the default rule set with a synthesized guard that survived an adversarial sweep. The same machinery honestly refused its apparent siblings, its first composed atom (pay-null), and its own compression layer (reach-null). Three measured blockers now stand between &quot;mints and ships&quot; and &quot;mints, ships, and <em>pays at scale</em>&quot;:</p><ol><li><strong>Enumeration ordering.</strong> The paying <code>fold_emit</code> descriptor sits <blockquote><p>200k deep in <code>propose_bodies</code>&#39; round-robin; it verifies at 6.7e-16 when reached directly. The gap is ordering, not expressiveness (<code>feat/enum-order</code> in flight).</p></blockquote></li><li><strong>Grammar dead space and gaps.</strong> <code>fold</code>/<code>fold_emit</code> empty-side const fillers always raise in <code>eval_body</code> (candidates that structurally cannot evaluate); reductions/softmax have zero candidates; the <code>a≡1</code> side is only spellable as <code>div(X,X)</code>, which the disjoint a/b partition can never propose; <code>_family_gens</code> hard-gates fold/fold_emit at ≥3 metas.</li><li><strong>Proposal space.</strong> Yield in the exposed corpus is ~1.5%, and the form list is still hand-written (plan 0024&#39;s remaining half). The combinator presentation (ADR 0008) is the uniform space, but gate 3 — whether search <em>reaches</em> <code>loop</code> forms — is unmeasured.</li></ol><h2 id="what-exists-don-t-rebuild" tabindex="-1">What exists (don&#39;t rebuild) <a class="header-anchor" href="#what-exists-don-t-rebuild" aria-label="Permalink to “What exists (don&#39;t rebuild)”">​</a></h2><ul><li><code>catopt_discovery.handler_synth</code> — the structured handler grammar + <code>verify_body</code> + <code>mint_handlers</code> + record round-trip (ADR 0007 L2).</li><li><code>lab/mint/atom_law_loop.py</code> — per-atom law synthesis (25 certified rows, 4 rejected, 0 refused) (ADR 0007 L3).</li><li><code>lab/mint/atom_synth_loop.py</code> — the composed need → handler → laws → admission → pay loop, with the stage-level funnel.</li><li><code>lab/bridge/combinator.py</code> / <code>combinator_probe.py</code> — the bridge, <code>BASIS</code> as data, both gates + the corpus round-trip driver.</li><li><code>catopt_discovery.enumerate</code> / <code>forms</code> (plan 0024) — instance and skeleton enumeration; the attr-spelling fix (<code>feat/enum-attr-gap</code>, 0→198 fires, 0 paying).</li><li>The admission gauntlet — oracle → typed pay gate → certificate replay → adversarial sweep → measured pay; unchanged throughout.</li></ul><h2 id="the-work" tabindex="-1">The work <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-work" aria-label="Permalink to “The work”">​</a></h2><h3 id="a-make-the-paying-descriptor-reachable-in-flight" tabindex="-1">A. Make the paying descriptor reachable (in flight) <a class="header-anchor" href="#a-make-the-paying-descriptor-reachable-in-flight" aria-label="Permalink to “A. Make the paying descriptor reachable (in flight)”">​</a></h3><p>Canonical emitted-scan seed in <code>propose_bodies</code>; stop emitting candidates whose const fillers cannot evaluate; re-measure the <code>SelectiveScan</code> funnel. <strong>Success = the minted atom&#39;s law set fires on real corpus terms</strong> (the pay question), or a named next blocker.</p><h3 id="b-grammar-extension-measured" tabindex="-1">B. Grammar extension, measured <a class="header-anchor" href="#b-grammar-extension-measured" aria-label="Permalink to “B. Grammar extension, measured”">​</a></h3><p>Extend the handler grammar by the <em>refusals</em>, not by taste: reductions/softmax (0 candidates today), an <code>a≡1</code> spelling that does not need <code>div(X,X)</code>, and an emit tree deeper than 1 non-acc op. Each extension lands with its refusal count dropping — measured.</p><h3 id="c-gate-3-—-does-search-reach-loop-forms" tabindex="-1">C. Gate 3 — does search reach <code>loop</code> forms? <a class="header-anchor" href="#c-gate-3-—-does-search-reach-loop-forms" aria-label="Permalink to “C. Gate 3 — does search reach loop forms?”">​</a></h3><p>The substrate&#39;s open question. On a corpus workload whose export erased a recurrence (<code>lstm.input</code>, <code>cumsum</code>, <code>cumprod</code>), run saturation over the <em>combinator</em> presentation and ask whether a <code>loop</code>-headed member appears and is extractable. If yes: the substrate is a discovery surface. If no: the fold must be proposed (the proposer carries the burden), and ADR 0008&#39;s cost is a presentation-only win — recorded either way.</p><h3 id="d-the-missing-law-families-birefnet-s-lesson" tabindex="-1">D. The missing law families (BiRefNet&#39;s lesson) <a class="header-anchor" href="#d-the-missing-law-families-birefnet-s-lesson" aria-label="Permalink to “D. The missing law families (BiRefNet&#39;s lesson)”">​</a></h3><p>The measured boundary: models whose math is already fused expose nothing to the op-algebra laws. Three families are named and untried — take them in cost order:</p><ol><li><strong>Precision</strong> — the bounded lane is <em>built</em> and was a certified negative on BiRefNet for a measured reason (thin dedup: the bounded member priced 1.32× worse than dense). Next target: a model where the dedup is thick (a wide-MLP checkpoint), and weight-space members rather than row-gather ones.</li><li><strong>Data movement</strong> — hoisting invariant structure (Swin masks are recomputed per layer, identical). Compete with Inductor here at your peril: measure <em>before</em> building.</li><li><strong>Weight space</strong> — conv+BN fusion targets exist (43 <code>BatchNorm2d</code> modules measured in real BiRefNet). Per the no-hardcoding rule, the work is <strong>derive-or-refuse</strong>: feed measured <code>(W,b,μ,σ,γ,β) → (W′,b′)</code> bindings to <code>dspec_synth</code> and let the machinery attempt the fold spec; whatever it cannot express becomes a named grammar gap (extend the grammar, never hand-write the law).</li></ol><h2 id="falsification" tabindex="-1">Falsification <a class="header-anchor" href="#falsification" aria-label="Permalink to “Falsification”">​</a></h2><ul><li>A: if the canonical seed is reached and the laws still fire nowhere real, the pay-null is semantic (the corpus&#39;s usages are in the guarded-out region) — record it and stop chasing the atom.</li><li>B: an extension that adds candidates without dropping a refusal count is churn — revert it.</li><li>C: gate 3 negative closes the substrate&#39;s <em>discovery</em> value; the presentation value (uniformity, explicit Δ) must then carry the ADR alone.</li><li>D: each family is killed by its own measurement (no pays → the family is closed with numbers, like the bounded lane&#39;s BiRefNet negative).</li></ul><h2 id="order" tabindex="-1">Order <a class="header-anchor" href="#order" aria-label="Permalink to “Order”">​</a></h2><p>A (in flight) → B → D1 (cheapest, machinery exists) → C → D3 (derive-or-refuse) → D2 (only with a measured reason).</p>`,21)]])}var s=n(a,[[`render`,o]]);export{i as __pageData,s as default};